# shipdoc-extract: structured extraction from shipping documents

{{auto:banner}}

{{auto:legend}} Report date {{values.report_date}}, commit {{values.commit_sha}}.

## 1. Approach and why

The target is accuracy on supplier layouts the system has never seen, so the primary metric is leave-supplier-out out-of-fold (OOF) OVERALL with K=3 supplier-grouped folds ({{values.suppliers_per_fold}} suppliers per fold), not the official dev score, which measures seen layouts. Invoice-only OOF is the headline because waybill groups (carrier brand) do not track layout. The model is Qwen3.5-4B, {{values.model_state}}. The safety architecture has three parts: (a) verbatim extraction: values are copied from the page and schema-repaired deterministically, never inferred; (b) a verifier that scores each field from token log-probabilities, OCR support, validators and cross-page agreement; (c) nulls come from the model. A calibrated-null policy (null iff P(gold null) exceeds P(value correct)) was tested and REJECTED for row fields because it lowered OVERALL ({{calibration.row_null_policy.delta|dci}} points, paired CI; header nulls unchanged). Reviewer routing uses per-field-type thresholds chosen by nested out-of-fold selection for at least 98% auto-accept precision; that target is met for header fields, approached but not met at the point estimate for the supplier part number, and out of reach for the other row fields and at document level (see the review-flag section for the numbers).

