## 3. Ablation ladder (paired deltas)

Each rung adds one component to the previous one; deltas are paired doc-level bootstraps on the same {{ablation.n_docs|int}} documents ({{ablation.split}}). Rules that change no value on this data are kept as fail-closed safety nets for unseen suppliers and no benefit is claimed for them.

{{table:ablation}}

## 4. Post-processing rules (R1-R3)

Deterministic merge rules run after extraction; a rule ships only if the paired CI of its OVERALL delta excludes zero with no broken cell. R1 fills a null waybill carrier from the model's own supplier-name slot. R2 backfills a null MAWB/HAWB from a unique OCR pattern match. R3 moves customer-part and PO values into the slot whose format shape they match. Gate evidence (R1, R2 on {{rules.train_docs|int}} train docs; R3 supplier-held-out on {{rules.r3_docs|int}} docs), cells fixed / broken and OVERALL delta in points: R1 {{rules.r1.fixed|int}} / {{rules.r1.broken|int}}, {{rules.r1.delta|dci}}; R2 {{rules.r2.fixed|int}} / {{rules.r2.broken|int}}, {{rules.r2.delta|dci}}; R3 {{rules.r3.fixed|int}} / {{rules.r3.broken|int}}, {{rules.r3.delta|dci}}. All three together through the production path: {{rules.combined.delta|dci}} points. R2 needs OCR at inference, a deployment cost; the OCR-free variant fixes {{rules.r2_ocrfree.fixed|int}} cells. **R3 disclosure:** its gains are concentrated: {{rules.r3.top3_fixed|int}} of {{rules.r3.total_fixed|int}} fixed rows come from {{rules.r3.top_n|int}} of {{rules.r3.groups_total|int}} invoice groups ({{rules.r3.groups_touched|int}} touched). The learned shapes equal the all-gold set in {{calibration.shapes_equal_folds|int}} of {{calibration.shapes_folds|int}} folds, so the supplier-held-out gate cannot show leakage but also cannot show transfer to a new format; R3 is judged only on folds where it fires.

## 5. Failure analysis

Diagnosed on dev run {{failure.run_id}} ({{failure.n_docs|int}} docs, a smaller set than the train+dev docs used elsewhere) from the row/header error taxonomy. Recoverable points are ORACLE upper bounds (the cause replaced by gold), not achievable gains.

- **Part-number misreads** ({{failure.causes.spn_misread.rows|int}} rows, {{failure.causes.spn_misread.docs|int}} docs; oracle {{failure.causes.spn_misread.oracle|dci}} points). Root cause: the right line is read with one or two wrong characters; the OCR text is also wrong in part of the cases, so snapping to the nearest OCR span breaks as many rows as it fixes (rule R4). Fix: glyph-level fine-tuning targets for part numbers.
- **Column shift on continuation pages** ({{failure.causes.column_shift.rows|int}} rows, {{failure.causes.column_shift.docs|int}} docs; oracle {{failure.causes.column_shift.oracle|dci}} points). Root cause: continuation pages carry no column-header row, so the model guesses the column order and values land one slot off; the contrast holds inside supplier groups. Fix: pass the first-page column order to continuation pages and train on continuation-page rows.
- **PO written into the customer-part slot** ({{failure.causes.po_in_cpn_slot.rows|int}} rows; oracle {{failure.causes.po_in_cpn_slot.oracle|dci}} points). Root cause: layouts without a customer-part column and with a PO column. Fix: a prompt/fine-tune target that leaves the slot null, or the format-shape swap rule R3 (its shapes are format shapes learned from the gold of the other suppliers, not synthetic formats).

## 6. A new supplier arrives tomorrow

On the first day: zero-config extraction; low-confidence fields go to a human reviewer. Reviewer corrections feed an active-learning queue. Any fine-tuned adapter would be refreshed periodically and adopted only if it beats the zero-shot-plus-rules system on three-fold out-of-fold evaluation (pre-registered rule in the spec's closing plan). Drift is monitored per layout cluster (review rate and null rate); the label-free cluster diagnostic on the test set found {{clusters.n_clusters|int}} invoice layout clusters over {{clusters.n_test_docs|int}} documents, with a raw unseen-layout flag share of {{clusters.estimated_unseen_share|pctp}} (a proxy that misses most truly unseen suppliers) and a predicted review rate of {{clusters.predicted_review_rate|pctp}}.

## 7. Review flag

A field is auto-accepted when P(correct) clears a per-field-type threshold chosen by nested out-of-fold selection (each fold's threshold is chosen on the other folds) for at least 98% auto-accept precision; coverage at the 95% and 99% targets is also shown. Coverage is the share of emitted fields auto-accepted. Status: attained; near-miss (point precision under target, CI contains it); NOT ATTAINABLE (precision under target, or coverage under {{calibration.min_coverage|pctp}}). ECE is the expected calibration error of P(correct). Only header fields and the supplier part number come within reach of the target; the other row fields and the document level go to review.

{{table:review}}

Caveats: the dev slice has only {{calibration.dev_docs|int}} docs, so its intervals are wide and it is not a separate test (the table pools zero-shot outputs on all {{calibration.n_docs|int}} train+dev docs, with calibrators cross-fitted by supplier folds); CIs resample documents but condition on the selected thresholds.

