## Honest limitations and what would fix each

- Dev is small (n={{dev.slices.all.documents|int}}, CI half-width {{dev.OVERALL_ci95|ciw}} points) and has seen layouts. Fix: report the OOF headline and re-gate on a larger held-out supplier set.
- Waybill groups track carrier brand, not layout, so waybill OOF is not an unseen-layout estimate. Fix: cluster waybills by an OCR layout signature and fold on clusters.
- Row part numbers depend on OCR quality for scanned pages and for the verifier's OCR-support feature. Fix: a stronger OCR or a scan-augmented fine-tune.
- Each fold has only {{values.suppliers_per_fold}} suppliers, so fold-level estimates are noisy. Fix: more suppliers per fold or repeated grouped splits.
- The fine-tuned system is adopted only if it beats the zero-shot-plus-rules system on three-fold out-of-fold evaluation (pre-registered rule); no fine-tuned claim is made from fewer than K=3 scored folds. Fix: train and score the remaining folds before the final claim.
- R3 gains are concentrated in a few invoice groups and its learned shapes do not differ across folds, so transfer to a new format is untested. Fix: evaluate on a held-out supplier whose format is not in train; collect more suppliers.
- Calibration CIs condition on the selected thresholds, and the calibrator model choice used the reported cross-fitted predictions. Fix: an outer holdout.
- The production pipeline needs OCR at inference for R2. Fix: OCR-free recovery or a model that reads those fields.
- Timing is {{cost.timing_basis}}, on shared Colab hardware without repeats, and the native-resolution cost is an estimate. Fix: repeat the runs and measure the final pipeline on a T4 at batch size {{cost.batch_size|int}}.
- The zoom re-read of small print is future work: it is not part of the submitted pipeline and no result is claimed for it. Fix: build and gate it on held-out suppliers.
- The inference environment lacks the causal-convolution and flash-linear-attention kernels and runs the reference fallback; faster kernels are a latency lever that is UNVERIFIED (no measurement exists). Fix: install them and re-measure latency and accuracy.
- Review-flag precision is bounded by calibrator quality on small per-type counts. Fix: collect reviewer decisions as labels and recalibrate per layout cluster.
